              "end": 15
            }
          ],
          "decisions": [
            {
              "id": "one-place-hides",
              "claim": "A new Conversation kind that lists must hide can be added by changing only listedConversation().",
              "concern": "Stats, locations, and direct Conversation page reads do not call it, so a hidden kind could still show up there.",
              "origin": { "kind": "assumed" }
            }
          ],
          "asks": [
            "Why is this a function and not a constant SQL value?",
            "Does the Conversation page use this filter?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "feed-and-token",
          "label": "Feed rows and change token",
          "caption": "The feed query and its change token now use the same filter, so they cannot drift apart.",
          "body": "The feed rows used to repeat both conditions by hand [1], and so did the change-token query [3]. Both now call `listedConversation()` [2][4]. The token tells clients when the feed changed. If its filter drifted from the rows, a hidden Quick question could change the token without changing the visible feed. Now the two match by construction.",
